9{y}^{2n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535230 17592186045417 true] [17592186139725 1064 "The **difference of squares formula** states the product of the sum and the difference of two monomials is equal to the difference of their squares:\n\n$$\n(a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\n$$\n\nWe can check that this result is correct by expanding the binomial in the usual way, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} ({\\color{blue}a} + {\\color{red}b})(a - b) \\\\[5pt] &= {\\color{blue}a}(a - b) + {\\color{red}b}(a - b) \\\\[5pt] &= a^2 - ab + ab - b^2 \\\\[5pt] &= a^2 - b^2 \\,& {\\color{green}{\\checkmark}} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the middle two terms $-ab$ and $ab$ cancel each other out, leaving only $a^2 - b^2$.\n\nIf the order of multiplication is switched, the formula still remains the same:\n\n$$\n(a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\n$$" 13194139535230 17592186045417 false] [17592186139725 1064 "The **difference of squares formula** states the product of the sum and the difference of two monomials is equal to the difference of their squares:\n\n$$\n(a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\n$$\n\nWe can check that this result is correct by expanding the binomial in the usual way, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t({\\color{blue}a} + {\\color{red}b})(a - b) &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t{\\color{blue}a}(a - b) + {\\color{red}b}(a - b) &= \\[5pt]\n\t\ta^2 - ab + ab - b^2 &= \\[5pt]\n\t\ta^2 - b^2 \\,& {\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n\t}\n$$\n\nNotice that the middle two terms $- ab$ and $ab$ cancel each other out, leaving only $a^2 - b^2.$ \n\nIf the order of multiplication is switched, the formula still remains the same:\n\n$$\n(a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\n$$" 13194139535230 17592186045417 true] [17592186147415 1038 #edb/ref 17592186483357 13194139535230 17592186045417 true] [17592186152160 1038 #edb/ref 17592186483379 13194139535230 17592186045417 true] [17592186152743 1068 #edb/ref 17592186150965 13194139535230 17592186045417 false] [17592186162073 1038 #edb/ref 17592186483349 13194139535230 17592186045417 