}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\theta )-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{i}!) \\\\  & =-\\theta {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{i}!) \\\\  & =-n\\theta +\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}!)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the sample data with $n=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}! & =3!\\cdot 4!\\cdot 2!=6\\cdot 24\\cdot 2=288, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =3+4+2=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting the above values into our expression for $l(\\theta ),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l(\\theta ) & =-3\\theta +9\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡288.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\na+b+c=-3+9+288=294.\n$$" 13194139535230 17592186045417 true] [17592186229163 1038 #edb/ref 17592186483350 13194139535230 17592186045417 true] [17592186233791 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483337 13194139535230 17592186045417 true] [17592186234405 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483333 13194139535230 17592186045417 true] [17592186243938 1071 "$$\n{A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Find the matrix $C$ given that $B=\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $B$ are $[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535230 17592186045417 true] [17592186243938 1071 "$$\n{A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Find the matrix $C$ given that $B={{A}_{1},{A}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}},$ and the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $B$ are $[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535230 17592186045417 false] [17592186243938 1074 "