btain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 12 & -2 & 0 & 18\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}-3\\cdot 2=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-6{x}_{1}+(-3)=-9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{2}=-3.$" 13194139535230 17592186045417 true] [17592186366601 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(-6{t}^{3}+6t+12)+{x}_{2}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-3t-2)+{x}_{3}(-3{t}^{2}+2t) & =-9{t}^{3}+19t+18 \\\\ (-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){t}^{3}+(-2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+(6{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})t+(12{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}) & =-9{t}^{3}+19t+18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=19 \\\\ 12{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 12 & -2 & 0 & 18\\end{aligned}].\